# i18n — no hardcoded UI copy

**Never** put user-visible English (or any language) as a raw string in markup, props, toasts, errors, placeholders, `aria-label`, `title`, or button labels in `packages/app` or `packages/website`. Always wrap with `t()` and add the key to all three locale files.

The **English sentence is the key**. Locales: `en`, `es`, `ko` in `packages/i18n/locales/`.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { useI18n } from '$lib/i18n';

	const { t } = useI18n();
</script>

<!-- ❌ BAD — hardcoded UI copy -->
<button>Upload</button>
<p>No results found.</p>
<Input placeholder="Search player..." />

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<button>{t('Upload')}</button>
<p>{t('No results found.')}</p>
<Input placeholder={t('Search player...')} />
<p>{t('{count} matches', { count })}</p>
```

```json
// en.json / es.json / ko.json — same key in all three
"Upload": "Upload",
"No results found.": "No results found.",
"{count} matches": "{count} matches"
```

## Checklist (every new/changed user string)

1. Call `t('English key')` (or `locals.t` on website server)
2. Add the key to **en.json, es.json, and ko.json**
3. Translate es/ko; if unsure, copy English so the key exists
4. Params use `{name}` in the key, passed as `{ name }` to `t()`

## Hosts vs `packages/ui`

- **App / website**: always `t()` — never hardcode
- **`packages/ui`**: English default label props only; hosts pass `t('…')` when wrapping. Do not import `$lib/i18n` inside `ui`
- App: module singleton (`ssr = false`). Website: per-request on `locals` (never a module singleton)

## Allowed without `t()`

- Technical identifiers (route ids, collection names, CSS classes, enum values, API field names)
- Developer-only logs / comments
- Content that is already translated elsewhere (`POLICY.md`, user-generated text, player names)

## Do not

- Ship UI copy only in a Svelte file without locale keys
- Invent a second i18n system or translate only `en.json`
- Hardcode strings in app/website “temporarily” and skip locales
